WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.620
- Hey everyone, it's Jasmine,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.140
and I love hosting dinner parties.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.340
And as much fun as it is

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.560
to get all your friends
together to entertain,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.300
I know it can be a little bit stressful,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.530
a little bit daunting.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.440
So today I'm gonna show you
some easy foolproof tips

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.940
so you can host like a pro.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.005
Let's get started.

00:00:16.005 --> 00:00:18.588
(bright music)

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.150
So it's the day before the dinner party,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.770
and we're gonna make a few crafts

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.600
to decorate our dinner table.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.450
We're first gonna be making
these clay napkin rings

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.000
and then these clay candle holders.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.833
They're super cute

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.210
and add a personalized
touch to your dinner table.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.520
So we're gonna start by
making our clay napkin rings.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.200
I have two colors of clay here.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.550
This one's the white,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.780
and I'm just gonna add
a few globs to my board.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.630
And then some terracotta clay here.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.310
Just sprinkle it, randomize it.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.560
It'll all look beautiful once together.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.790
That looks good.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.430
So we're gonna place
it back onto our board

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.343
and we're just gonna roll it
out to a quarter inch thick.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.103
Okay, uh.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.200
Looks good now.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.310
So now we have a ruler here.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.777
I'm just gonna place it right here.

00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:10.170
And we're just gonna draw a
straight line all the way down.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.360
Same thing on the other side.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.730
Now we're just gonna cut
this down on either side

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.440
so we have straight lines.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.790
We're gonna cut this in half.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.230
Now we're gonna take either side,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.330
overlap it, and just pinch it close.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.560
Ta-da!

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.660
Super easy, super cute.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.660
Truly, there's no way to mess this up.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.960
And we're just gonna let
it air-dry overnight.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.190
With my scraps here,

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.200
I'm gonna combine this into a ball

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.600
and show you how I make my candle holders.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.580
We're just gonna roll this
up into a nice fine sphere.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.460
I split my ball into two.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.410
And I'm just rounding these out.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.850
And we're gonna take our candle

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.160
and stick it directly inside.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.890
And since it air dries
a little bit smaller,

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.810
you wanna kind of roll it out

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.380
so there's a little more space
and it will fit tomorrow.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.630
We're gonna do the same
thing with this one

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.920
and we're gonna let it dry overnight.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.810
I actually made some yesterday.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.990
So once these air dry,
they'll look like this.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.100
They're super cute.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.510
They just look very rustic.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.400
You know, I'd buy something
like this off Etsy.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.930
It's super artsy.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.300
And it just adds that extra touch

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.950
to your hosted dinner party.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.370
So the next craft we're gonna
be making is ice dyed napkins.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.660
Super cool, super easy.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.090
We're gonna start with a
baking sheet on the bottom

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.220
and a wire rack over a tray.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.560
And I have a couple of damp napkins here.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.530
We're just gonna scrunch
them up ever so slightly

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.003
over the tray.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.170
Do the same with your other napkin.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.720
This one is super cool
and really easy, honestly.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.570
And same thing with this
one, you can't mess up.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.730
It'll look amazing, promise.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.770
And you can customize it
to your favorite colors,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.603
which is also great.

00:02:47.603 --> 00:02:48.720
So if you're doing a themed party

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.370
and you have colors, go ahead and do that.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.750
Now that these are all scrunched up,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.933
I'm gonna place a bunch
of ice all over them.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.190
Feel free to be generous with this.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.600
And make sure to wear gloves

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.880
because working with dye,
you may stain in your hands.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.490
Now we're gonna sprinkle
on some powdered dye,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.700
blues and greens, in random spots.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.743
Moving on to my next color here.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.650
And just be free spirited with this.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.900
It'll turn out beautiful, I promise.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.060
So when the ice starts to melt,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.310
it'll leave this really
cool tie dye effect.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.890
And that's what's gonna
give it that design.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.240
Now that I've done all of this,

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.260
I'm gonna bring this outside,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.990
let all the ice melt, then let it air dry,

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.360
bring it back in, run it under the sink

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.240
until all the color runs
clear before washing it.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.450
I made some yesterday and
this is what it looks like.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.340
Look how cool it is.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.440
It's kind of like this aqua marine vibe.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.360
I really like the coastal look.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.860
They're beautiful.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.510
And they just add a pop of
color to the dinner table.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.500
So it's the day of the dinner party.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.360
Our guests are arriving in a few hours,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.330
and we're gonna begin our flower
arrangements for the table.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.700
You can use some flower frogs here.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.680
We have glass and a metal one,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.570
but they also come in different materials.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.280
And you can also use these bud vases

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.160
for simple and really
adorable arrangements.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:05.993
Look at these.

00:04:05.993 --> 00:04:07.020
I love them.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.250
So one hack I have

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.320
is to pull the vase close to the table,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.820
hold your flower against it

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.100
to see what height you'd
like it to stand at.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.870
And then we're just
gonna cut out a diagonal.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.880
Today, we're gonna be using the metal frog

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.110
and it'll go inside the vase,

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.550
but I'll demonstrate out here.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.200
All you do is put it in your desired place

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.340
and shove it right in,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.510
and it'll stay intact.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.030
I'm just gonna pick this up
and put it into our vase.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.510
And I have some tack on
the bottom to hold it down.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.240
So what I like to do is start
with some show stoppers.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.620
That looks good.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.600
So now I have some other flowers

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.970
and I'm just gonna fill them in

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.280
and get it all evenly dispersed.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.840
I really love that the flower frogs

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.160
keep everything in place.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.130
And I like to get flowers with
different kinds of textures.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.260
It just makes it look more vibrant.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.370
And there you have it.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.950
A beautiful flower arrangement
is gonna stay in its place.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.280
And last thing we're gonna
do is add in some water.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.113
Beautiful.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.850
Okay, it's time to set the
table for our dinner party.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.560
Today we have four people coming,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.360
and we're gonna be having a main

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.330
with a salad, wine, and water.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.370
So we're gonna start with a large plate

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.770
with a salad plate on top.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.500
We have a cute little
handmade menu right here,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.250
and this just adds a little
extra to the dinner table.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.530
Got some cute little
hand drawn art on there

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.700
and just a good overall view

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.700
of what everyone will be
eating at the dinner party.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.470
Next we got our hand dyed napkins

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.810
and our handmade napkin ring.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.270
We're just gonna place it on top.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.410
Next we got our utensils.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.170
The solid fork will be
on the outer left side

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:41.130
and the main fork will be
on the inner left side,

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.180
and our knife on the right side

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.640
with the blade facing towards the plates.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.473
For our cups,

00:05:45.473 --> 00:05:48.000
we're gonna place the
water glass above the knife

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.790
and our wine glass just
to the right of that.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:51.720
And there you have it.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.190
The table is set.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:54.540
It looks complicated

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.490
but it was actually pretty easy to do

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.260
and very straightforward.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.703
Now onto the food.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:01.770
So now I'm gonna show you

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.260
how I like to display
the dishes on the table.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.320
For starters, I really love
this Mediterranean hummus.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.050
This is an awesome way to
upgrade some store bought hummus,

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.170
and just display it
differently and beautifully.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.450
So I've already laid out some hummus here

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.670
with some rainbow carrots on the side.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.140
And we're just gonna add some toppings

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.030
to make it extra fancy.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.430
First, I'm gonna lay out
some cucumber slices,

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.620
adds a nice crunch to everything,

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.810
nice and vibrant, and just add some color.

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.540
Next I'm gonna add in
some sun-dried tomatoes.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.670
I love the red it brings to this dish.

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.040
Next we're gonna top it with some feta,

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.390
just a nightlight sprinkle.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.910
Ooh, that looks so pretty.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.520
Next we're gonna top
it with some pine nuts.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.220
Yes, we are going very fancy here.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.540
And some mint.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.480
Last but not least, we're gonna
drizzle on some olive oil.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.580
There you have it, some
Mediterranean hummus.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.340
I love the vibrancy of
the toppings on here.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.697
People are gonna look at this and say,

00:06:54.697 --> 00:06:56.430
"Wow, let me take a photo of that."

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:57.263
And that's the goal.

00:06:57.263 --> 00:06:58.440
These are all done.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.813
I'm gonna place them right over here.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:02.970
Beautiful.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.740
So another appetizer I love

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.590
are these fig and whipped
ricotta crostinis.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.350
They're so, so cute and delicious.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.000
Figs are in season right now.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.820
And whenever I can use
local and in season produce

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.640
when hosting others, that's an extra plus.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:18.870
These are so good.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.150
The whipped ricotta is so fluffy,

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.730
topped with the honey and balsamic glaze.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.040
Ugh, so, so delicious.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.780
So for the show-stopping main,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.190
I love to make this beef
tenderloin paired with fresh herbs,

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.440
a creamy horseradish dressing.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.380
One thing I love to do
is slice them beforehand,

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.320
plate it with some fresh herbs,
and the sauce on the side.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.540
That way no one needs to
worry about cutting the meat.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.780
And honestly, it makes for
some really great presentation.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:48.150
One of my favorite sides
to make for dinner parties

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:51.030
are these gorgeous potato roses.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.280
This is just a really fun and unique way

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.790
to elevate the presentation
of roasted potatoes.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.620
And while they look super
complicated to make,

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.260
they're actually pretty
easy for beginners.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.170
And I just love to place
them on a cake dish

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:07.110
so it looks like another bouquet
of flowers on your table.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:08.760
All right, time for some salad.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.100
I love to add a big salad to my table

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.690
when I'm hosting a dinner party.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.120
Honestly, we need some greens.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.130
I love to add in some fresh fruit,

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.050
some nuts for texture,

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.060
very flavorful veggies like fennel.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.290
Got some onion.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.090
Avocado for creaminess.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.280
This is just overall a great way

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:30.033
to add vibrancy to the table
for presentation and in flavor.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.050
For dessert, I love to do a DIY parfait

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.430
for my dinner parties.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:38.250
It lets guests get creative
and customized to their liking,

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.230
and also give them a taste of everything.

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.760
You can display it however you like,

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.590
but for me I love to use a variety

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:45.360
of different colorful bowls.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.190
I've already built some
over here on the table.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:50.730
I added some of my favorites,
which was all of them.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.590
All the brownies, all the cheesecake,

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.970
berries, fudge, caramel,

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.710
chocolate chips, literally everything,

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.720
'cause that's what makes it taste so good.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.180
I also added some whipped cream on top.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.530
This is just one way to do it,

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:02.790
but you can get really creative

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.020
and come up with different themes.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.670
You can do ice cream sundaes.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.230
Chocolate fondue, honestly.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.180
The possibilities are endless.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.640
Final setup for dinner is complete.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:14.280
I lit some candles, poured some water,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.960
and of course, some wine.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.190
Cheers.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.840
All right, I hope these tips were helpful

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:20.250
and show that with just a little bit

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.870
of preparation and creativity,

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.390
anyone can throw their first
dinner party like a pro.

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.470
Let me know in the comments below

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.144
if you have any dinner
party tips to share.

00:09:27.144 --> 00:09:27.977
(bell rings)

00:09:27.977 --> 00:09:29.640
Oh my, my guests are here.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.241
Uh, you got this, bye!

00:09:31.241 --> 00:09:33.824
(bright music)

